--------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository bundles no third-party source code and has no software
dependencies beyond the Lean 4 toolchain and the Python standard library.
Lean 4 (https://github.com/leanprover/lean4) is itself Apache-2.0 licensed
and is fetched at build time rather than vendored here.

DATA

All example data in this repository is synthetic or constructed by the
author. Specifically:

  gridcert/examples/study.json
      A five-bus test network whose topology follows the widely published
      PJM 5-bus educational example, a teaching case that appears in
      textbooks and course materials without restriction. Branch
      reactances have been rounded so that each susceptance is an integer;
      the largest resulting change is under one percent. Ratings, the
      injection box and the interconnection request are invented by the
      author for illustration. No utility, ISO/RTO, or client data is
      present.

  carbonsched/examples/scenarios.json
      Marginal carbon intensity profiles shaped by hand to resemble a
      summer weekday load shape. These are illustrative and are NOT
      measured data from any grid operator or emissions provider. See
      docs/LIMITATIONS.md.

  tolstack/examples/axial_gap.json
      An invented bearing-and-spacer stack-up. Not taken from any drawing.

  lyapcert/examples/systems.json
      Invented discrete-time systems chosen to exercise the certificate
      paths, including a marginally stable and a deadbeat case.

  dimcert/examples/interconnection.json
      Textbook power-system relations. The SI base and derived dimensions
      encoded in dimcert/DimCert/Units.lean follow the International
      System of Units as published by the BIPM, which is factual reference
      data and not subject to copyright.
